@page
@model IndexModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Home page";
}

<div class="text-center">
    <h1 class="display-4">
        Bring CAVA to Stillwater, Oklahoma!
    </h1>
    <h2> We believe Stillwater, Oklahoma, would be a great place for CAVA to open its next location, and here are a few reasons why</h2>
</div>

<p>






    1. A Community That Loves Healthy Food

    Stillwater is home to Oklahoma State University, which had 27,655 students on its Stillwater campus in fall 2025. We have thousands of students, student-athletes, and people who enjoy staying active and eating healthy.

    We believe CAVA would be a great option for people looking for fresh, healthy meals, especially students and athletes who care about their nutrition.

    2. Not Much Competition

    Here in Stillwater, we have plenty of restaurants, but not many offer the same type of food as CAVA.

    There isn’t a franchise/chain style location for Mediterranean foods in Stillwater. Stillwater also lacks a location which provides “build your own” Mediterranean bowls.

    We think CAVA could bring something different to our community and become a popular option for students and local residents.

    3. CAVA Is Already Growing in Oklahoma

    CAVA already has 12 locations across Oklahoma, including restaurants in Norman, Tulsa, and Edmond.

    Norman is home to the University of Oklahoma, which has a similar college-town environment to Stillwater.

    We believe Stillwater could be another great location for CAVA, especially with the large student population and active community we have here.

    4. People in Oklahoma Already Enjoy CAVA

    Based on the reviews we’ve looked at, CAVA locations in Oklahoma have received ratings around 3.5–4 stars out of 5, although ratings vary by location.

    This shows us that people in Oklahoma are already familiar with CAVA, and we believe many people in Stillwater would enjoy having the same option closer to home.

    5. A Great Opportunity for Business

    Stillwater has an estimated population of 50,046 residents, along with a large university community.

    But Stillwater is not just about students. We also have families, working professionals, and thousands of visitors who come for OSU sporting events throughout the year.

    For example, Boone Pickens Stadium has a capacity of 52,202 people, showing how many visitors our city can attract during major football games.

    We believe CAVA could benefit from both the everyday demand from students and local residents and the additional customers who visit Stillwater for sporting events.


    Why We Want CAVA Here

    As students and members of the Stillwater community, we would love to have more healthy food options in town.

    With over 27,000 students, around 50,000 residents, limited direct competition, and a strong athletic community, we believe Stillwater has a lot of potential for CAVA.

    CAVA is already growing across Oklahoma, so why not Stillwater?

    We hope CAVA will consider Stillwater, Oklahoma, as one of its future locations!

    Bring CAVA to Stillwater

</p>